# PilotFish interface construction

When creating, scaffolding, expanding, or design-documenting a PilotFish interface under `Clients/`:

1. **Read and follow** `docs/INTERFACE_CONSTRUCTION_PLAYBOOK.md` end-to-end.
2. **Choose modules from** the external docs project at `/Users/brianhannan/Documents/PilotFish Documentation` (see `PilotFish_Documentation/DOCUMENTATION_LOCATION.txt`; use `Documents/` for tracker + deep dives) and `PilotFish_V2/` (`modules.conf` + `com/pilotfish/eip/modules` Java). EIP modules are shared with V1 — use that code to learn FQCNs and config items. Do not invent class names.
3. **Assemble runtime as V1** `pilotfish/demo-eip-root/**/route.xml` for `pilotfish-eip:23R1`. Copy a Sandbox demo skeleton when one exists for those classes. **Generate V2** (`route.v2.xml`) for Routes tab / PDF. `PilotFish_V2` is for module + format knowledge — not “author V2-only runtime” unless the user overrides.
4. **Do not invent** a one-off layout — after module selection, copy the closest demo (`edi-837-snip-sqlserver` or `hl7-healthcare-automation`) and delete unused pieces.
5. **Before coding:** capture pre-flight answers and create `DESIGN.md` from the playbook §8 template (include chosen FQCNs in the Pipeline table).
6. **No silent drift** between runtime V1 and diagram V2; call out doc/WAR version skew (e.g. 26R1 docs vs 23R1 image) in DESIGN.md.
7. **No compliance theater:** stages named Validate / SNIP / Split must gate, validate the wire artifact, or truly fork — otherwise rename and document.
8. **No hardcoded X12/HL7 wire text:** when generating EDI or HL7, XSLT builds PilotFish structured EDI XML / HL7 XML, then `EDITransformationProcessor` (`XML to EDI`) or `HL7TransformationProcessor` (`XML to HL7 2.X`). Never concatenate `ISA*…` or `MSH|…` as `xsl:output method="text"` for new work (playbook §3.5). `edi-278-prior-auth` is the demo reference.
9. **X12 TableData (required for EDI demos):** use repo-root `EDI/TableData/x12` (playbook §3.6 + `EDI/README.md`). Mount it to `eip-root/edi-tabledata`, set `UseInternalData=false` + `USE_ENHANCED_CONTEXT=true` + `TransactionDataWithVersion` → `edi-tabledata/<IG>` (`5010`). Prefer TableData `examples/*.edi` / XSDs when they improve the demo; keep story-specific `samples/` when logic depends on them.
10. **No claim-before-complete** and **no dual-write without compensation** unless explicitly listed as an accepted demo risk in `DESIGN.md`.
11. **Ship:** README (ports + smoke cmds), bounded polls/throttling for heavy stages, kickout/poison story, Web UI + route-viewer when routes are part of the deliverable (copy `diagram-groups.js` from `fhir-r4-platform`; prefer `config=compact` for committed route PDFs).
12. **Always generate the route design PDF** into `documents/`. For long processor chains (≥4 in a row or ≥8 on a worker), author `diagram-groups.json` and export **overview (collapsed groups) + later detail pages** per playbook §6.1b (`python3 tools/export_route_diagrams.py --config compact`). Do this for every new interface without waiting to be asked.
13. **LAN access (required on spin-up):** detect the host `192.*` address, keep Web UI published on `0.0.0.0` (not `127.0.0.1`-only), set compose `LAN_HINT=http://<192.x.x.x>:<webui-port>/`, and announce **both** localhost and LAN URLs in README + the agent summary whenever the UI is running.
14. **Browser links for every review PDF (required):** serve PDFs from the Web UI under `/documents/…` (mount `documents/`), verify HTTP 200 + `application/pdf` on the LAN IP, and paste **both** localhost and `http://192.x.x.x:<port>/documents/<file>.pdf` in the agent summary. Do not rely on Google Drive alone (credentials often expire); Drive upload is optional extra only.
15. **Done only after** smoke test (§7 of the playbook), grouped route PDF in `documents/` when §6.1b applies, LAN UI + PDF browser URLs configured/announced, and a plain-language list of limitations.
